==Results==
Enkhbayer secured more than 50% of the votes, thus winning an [[Landslide victory|outright victory]] in the first round and avoiding the need for a [[Run-off election|run-off]].<ref>{{cite news| url = http://www.smh.com.au/news/World/Former-communist-wins-Mongolian-elections/2005/05/23/1116700622136.html | title = Former communist wins Mongolian election | accessdate = 1 March 2009 | date = 23 May 2005 | newspaper = [[The Sydney Morning Herald]]}}</ref> After the results were announced, Enkhsaikhan called Enkhbayar to congratulate him on his victory, and they discussed working together.<ref name=communists/> Enkhbayar was [[inaugurate]]d as the 3rd [[President of Mongolia]] on 24 June and promised to fulfill the pledges that he had made during the campaign.<ref name=inaugurates/>

